{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "voices": [
    "en-US-AndrewNeural"
  ],
  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "12",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p12-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "b2db9697d5153b7795c40e152385ae2ce3d36f625475cfe3d0fa9d7dd22b0204",
        "2": "c425ea159e854afc2af3c0a2dd170811c5ada052d74b6ddb4ac8e72e1f81524c",
        "3": "b898c9a5731ffb71528a5c1de929536018c5e00ff59252b49accaa32d3c6ea85",
        "4": "265e95740d91a63d9cedec7a8e807e2af0978d79ed603dd41ac7b5d13d10c239"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s01-c1-2d890d6c85b5",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A web app needs to go from source code or a container image to a reachable service. App Runner's managed model builds or deploys it, gives it an H T T P S endpoint, and handles health checks and scaling for supported configurations.",
          "text_sha256": "2d890d6c85b5fe18730def69cbfcf082e9b1c417164ddb2b9de67eb53cf24b32",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e6eeddaea3644cd83a4cf38ece1918ebf02cff014040fb978908088ba90987d0",
          "asset_sha256": "b2db9697d5153b7795c40e152385ae2ce3d36f625475cfe3d0fa9d7dd22b0204"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s01-c2-7b9dd45977d3",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "But can a new customer choose it? No. App Runner is closed to new customers. For a similar managed path with a new workload, evaluate E C S Express Mode.",
          "text_sha256": "7b9dd45977d39bdfaf288c5cb7ddd46b3bd77a7c40f739c2561a93de39ccc8d4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2a40b4a23178026ec59e2a8cf6b07069bb826b0fdd3eb67656292fb4d6cf1a0b",
          "asset_sha256": "b2db9697d5153b7795c40e152385ae2ce3d36f625475cfe3d0fa9d7dd22b0204"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s02-c1-725bbd3f8045",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the team already uses App Runner, it can continue using supported services and create resources. Current eligibility matters more than whether the service appears in an architecture diagram.",
          "text_sha256": "725bbd3f8045e37c3854c6d3d7bbf59ea686e468f4948995880f3e17fda8d6f9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "725bbd3f8045e37c3854c6d3d7bbf59ea686e468f4948995880f3e17fda8d6f9",
          "asset_sha256": "c425ea159e854afc2af3c0a2dd170811c5ada052d74b6ddb4ac8e72e1f81524c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s02-c2-13359356d579",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For new customers, consider E C S Express Mode to deploy the web app from a container image. Check what network access, health checks and permissions the target needs.",
          "text_sha256": "13359356d579320eea18772a17c73f021c3d85bc6588beb713c2c38b34426004",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9bfa8d408bb8ea634da7c44a3219016407494c252b4bf562bf272a7b08b65087",
          "asset_sha256": "c425ea159e854afc2af3c0a2dd170811c5ada052d74b6ddb4ac8e72e1f81524c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s02-c3-70c17aa4e3dc",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For a migration, test the container on the new service, verify its endpoint and health, then shift traffic gradually with a rollback plan. Reusing the image does not automatically move the app's other dependencies.",
          "text_sha256": "70c17aa4e3dcfd6c557c560f26a2364a6f2f6c5971e32961bab7d65cd296373c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "70c17aa4e3dcfd6c557c560f26a2364a6f2f6c5971e32961bab7d65cd296373c",
          "asset_sha256": "c425ea159e854afc2af3c0a2dd170811c5ada052d74b6ddb4ac8e72e1f81524c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s03-c1-581c9effb022",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "An existing App Runner app needs a private database. The VPC connector routes the application's outbound traffic through selected private subnets and security groups. Check that the database allows the intended traffic.",
          "text_sha256": "581c9effb0226dfe8d225ec76bc4aa1b5cadb5038a68b819d43a6614e18f9e0f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "581c9effb0226dfe8d225ec76bc4aa1b5cadb5038a68b819d43a6614e18f9e0f",
          "asset_sha256": "b898c9a5731ffb71528a5c1de929536018c5e00ff59252b49accaa32d3c6ea85"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s03-c2-732cb6068c93",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "If the app also needs public internet egress, provide an appropriate nat path. For supported A W S services, endpoints may fit. Choosing a public subnet for the connector is not a shortcut to a public address.",
          "text_sha256": "732cb6068c93e7b3b5325095ba5eff06d2802c07ca570ec42497e4cfcd1467d9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "10814523858c66655992b352db1ad1bca846f3a3d1396753e93f7c4818b67e0b",
          "asset_sha256": "b898c9a5731ffb71528a5c1de929536018c5e00ff59252b49accaa32d3c6ea85"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s03-c3-d6dca10605c6",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Is the application private just because it can reach a private database? No. The outbound connector does not change ingress. Configure a public or supported private inbound endpoint separately.",
          "text_sha256": "d6dca10605c648f501d0da72f471e18b544d6b56210261d0fbea03eed277cb9e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d6dca10605c648f501d0da72f471e18b544d6b56210261d0fbea03eed277cb9e",
          "asset_sha256": "b898c9a5731ffb71528a5c1de929536018c5e00ff59252b49accaa32d3c6ea85"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s04-c1-bb7db84ef640",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "The client reaches a regional endpoint through the traffic layer. Check endpoint health, certificate behavior and cached D N S answers. A regional design still needs clients to reach the region you intend.",
          "text_sha256": "bb7db84ef6400779a8f711dbafb38e149d607eef27dd18808a32cee00e51c333",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4108d6ac9b48f4ed3053a33241c8f6fb7243515a6169beba0f7beeca9ed06b54",
          "asset_sha256": "265e95740d91a63d9cedec7a8e807e2af0978d79ed603dd41ac7b5d13d10c239"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s04-c2-06b00e1ec768",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "The app runs independently in each Region. Replicating the image gives the second deployment the same digest to pull, but it does not deploy the service or its configuration.",
          "text_sha256": "06b00e1ec768ce051a72038b9461fbbfee8975fddb3028c508d30885a81b1010",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "06b00e1ec768ce051a72038b9461fbbfee8975fddb3028c508d30885a81b1010",
          "asset_sha256": "265e95740d91a63d9cedec7a8e807e2af0978d79ed603dd41ac7b5d13d10c239"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p12-andrew-exp-s04-c3-5cd7e940561b",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "If the app uses global tables, choose the consistency model and what happens during concurrent writes. A healthy route and a matching container image do not prove that a second Region can serve the data correctly.",
          "text_sha256": "5cd7e940561b91081176134f487f6f6fd6e97f26d207c9db1a99bd58059397c2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5cd7e940561b91081176134f487f6f6fd6e97f26d207c9db1a99bd58059397c2",
          "asset_sha256": "265e95740d91a63d9cedec7a8e807e2af0978d79ed603dd41ac7b5d13d10c239"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "13",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p13-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "41363acd6ca16ad11d9b22a10449e5b22876f3b6958507687d5ce6f4efefe4e8",
        "2": "637b24b5ae81a1a941e05aabe15da96f1b69956e41d21664150771f0381211fe",
        "3": "f70a39b7c4fed4b96328c42f5b2af5b8804673b89cf5bfde0b1308aa09d26bc1",
        "4": "d46c0685a3d107806d3ee8f0664425ac08365fb531e8a217928c79d6bdfd8dde"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p13-andrew-exp-s01-c1-d40e1201040f",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The team has an on-premises host but wants A W S to schedule container work. E C S and Systems Manager supply the A W S control path; the registered, customer-managed host runs the external tasks.",
          "text_sha256": "d40e1201040fdd9a6dae077778e5633128b9d63c9c59fb28b87759ab2569ecce",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3e8da60234b7b35d101d94feca888e5b88170c0e6c7ed5d2f989de34d7c65cd6",
          "asset_sha256": "41363acd6ca16ad11d9b22a10449e5b22876f3b6958507687d5ce6f4efefe4e8"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p13-andrew-exp-s01-c2-a9950afe74e8",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "You still own the host, network and supported configuration. Existing tasks may keep running through a temporary disconnect, but reliable scheduling and management need the regional connection.",
          "text_sha256": "a9950afe74e8ce0fd6bf295e206445565906e82a75a3435e71a7659307d50061",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a9950afe74e8ce0fd6bf295e206445565906e82a75a3435e71a7659307d50061",
          "asset_sha256": "41363acd6ca16ad11d9b22a10449e5b22876f3b6958507687d5ce6f4efefe4e8"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p13-andrew-exp-s02-c1-eeba593ae4f5",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Register the external host with the supported agents so the control plane can see it. The team operates the host and its local network.",
          "text_sha256": "eeba593ae4f528f0f2387a5a9e5ff3060d8be7c34cc5d641eb335480d4cce283",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "eeba593ae4f528f0f2387a5a9e5ff3060d8be7c34cc5d641eb335480d4cce283",
          "asset_sha256": "637b24b5ae81a1a941e05aabe15da96f1b69956e41d21664150771f0381211fe"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p13-andrew-exp-s02-c2-766176bee481",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A W S E C S schedules external tasks on that host. Use a supported network mode, bridge, host or none. Do not assume normal E C S service load balancing, service discovery or capacity providers work for external tasks.",
          "text_sha256": "766176bee481a9ffaeaab0bdaf132b34c7b8fae07bae445e813879d217267817",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7ed05e9b0c27569c559d4c5b08bf78b7d4402499e2a84fd09b9b166a9425921c",
          "asset_sha256": "637b24b5ae81a1a941e05aabe15da96f1b69956e41d21664150771f0381211fe"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p13-andrew-exp-s02-c3-d9deec4255c1",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Running tasks can continue through some disconnects, but the regional control path cannot reliably manage and schedule new work until it reconnects. Test how operations behave in that gap.",
          "text_sha256": "d9deec4255c1e0297a115175f53f58f4fdc998c932469165a6e1c3a0ab91c87a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d9deec4255c1e0297a115175f53f58f4fdc998c932469165a6e1c3a0ab91c87a",
          "asset_sha256": "637b24b5ae81a1a941e05aabe15da96f1b69956e41d21664150771f0381211fe"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p13-andrew-exp-s03-c1-7bb316144179",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "E K S Anywhere takes a different approach: the koo ber NET ees control plane and workers live on customer infrastructure. The team operates that cluster and prepares its dependencies and upgrades.",
          "text_sha256": "7bb3161441793ae53babef92a05338421c65b696c256271523d5393de9cacf48",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "94c8bd0a4dea0dfed02b86a80a290733f14895dda766570316b60597d3c061aa",
          "asset_sha256": "f70a39b7c4fed4b96328c42f5b2af5b8804673b89cf5bfde0b1308aa09d26bc1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p13-andrew-exp-s03-c2-add39de8bc68",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The optional connector can add console visibility when connected. That does not move the koo ber NET ees control plane into A W S or make it A W S-managed E K S.",
          "text_sha256": "add39de8bc68f83132e9c4518141a4fb4b2544782f4e1d551636aba72eec1e19",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "89dd5f5858e622733f142413b7d3e25e08aa696cfbd31ff010c5c9b2c8d8de23",
          "asset_sha256": "f70a39b7c4fed4b96328c42f5b2af5b8804673b89cf5bfde0b1308aa09d26bc1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p13-andrew-exp-s04-c1-3b281deb5fa9",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "The control plane, workers and local registry can all stay inside the environment. Use a supported setup if the cluster has to operate without regular A W S connectivity.",
          "text_sha256": "3b281deb5fa99318f6e7b45a91d2b9a6319afcf3a03e44ff8df77ecd34c6fe2f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "64671ef327a05edb0e3f8e2a48e26d3a21daf4d066ceacf853edb280dafa7498",
          "asset_sha256": "d46c0685a3d107806d3ee8f0664425ac08365fb531e8a217928c79d6bdfd8dde"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p13-andrew-exp-s04-c2-a7053458ea31",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Download the approved images and dependencies ahead of time and mirror them to the local registry. Then verify deployment and upgrades through that disconnected path rather than assuming internet access at each step.",
          "text_sha256": "a7053458ea31217e5f95cf0f31300a7dff00bd445aff8d88c63abc0fe5183f0a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a7053458ea31217e5f95cf0f31300a7dff00bd445aff8d88c63abc0fe5183f0a",
          "asset_sha256": "d46c0685a3d107806d3ee8f0664425ac08365fb531e8a217928c79d6bdfd8dde"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "14",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p14-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "8e97c597079bb5b3f698a929217a8b59fc05f75cbf07f7d85af815b4cbac4b2d",
        "2": "63f9f3e13c7a1dccd0c266382593376b8cc64b65319166d2c0ee2c7e65cc2ce2",
        "3": "148837ba5f622a8cbbd275ef3da2a74eafb2cf4a6629b7cafa989635488b4ff7",
        "4": "b3f4519f7ea9747e3b6b3c7cce083c14be9ebcbadb207eba2763b9f48de205c5"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p14-andrew-exp-s01-c1-4ff21843e18a",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A backend's address can change when it is replaced. Register the instance and its relevant attributes and health information under a Cloud Map service so the lookup is not tied to yesterday's address.",
          "text_sha256": "4ff21843e18ae383e8c7ac03145a9051961565ef334e842ce599d539c869c535",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4ff21843e18ae383e8c7ac03145a9051961565ef334e842ce599d539c869c535",
          "asset_sha256": "8e97c597079bb5b3f698a929217a8b59fc05f75cbf07f7d85af815b4cbac4b2d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p14-andrew-exp-s01-c2-268d28aa68fc",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The client looks up the service using its configured D N S or A P I path and gets an eligible endpoint. It then makes a separate connection to the backend. Check caching and permissions for that connection.",
          "text_sha256": "268d28aa68fc91de6795d95af9c6de6aa8bb197a89cabcb49e00d3e35de56dd6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7d1e41af9668a48463467be539645cde3a6ab8e5b0638b1710e7d497724535ee",
          "asset_sha256": "8e97c597079bb5b3f698a929217a8b59fc05f75cbf07f7d85af815b4cbac4b2d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p14-andrew-exp-s02-c1-538a4f271edb",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The backend registers its address. Cloud Map answers the client's lookup. The data does not flow through Cloud Map; the client connects to the returned endpoint.",
          "text_sha256": "538a4f271edb3cf39586648c74ca8e34ce37adb252b97fe6ffa6cd1891f9cfc0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "538a4f271edb3cf39586648c74ca8e34ce37adb252b97fe6ffa6cd1891f9cfc0",
          "asset_sha256": "63f9f3e13c7a1dccd0c266382593376b8cc64b65319166d2c0ee2c7e65cc2ce2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p14-andrew-exp-s02-c2-46945ea9983f",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If a lookup succeeds but the connection fails, check the route, security rules and required permission. Also consider cached results and the configured health behavior.",
          "text_sha256": "46945ea9983fe4c247bb092df361e81a45c9ff3c395ee4cfd377402f7434968c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "46945ea9983fe4c247bb092df361e81a45c9ff3c395ee4cfd377402f7434968c",
          "asset_sha256": "63f9f3e13c7a1dccd0c266382593376b8cc64b65319166d2c0ee2c7e65cc2ce2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p14-andrew-exp-s03-c1-29bf85f756b4",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Service Connect gives participating E C S services stable short names through a Cloud Map namespace. The name stays useful even when tasks are replaced.",
          "text_sha256": "29bf85f756b4b32ee7433979b111f4ed8cb4a00ad759cce0d3fb82073911e8bb",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "95c94e28f04906b91bfe627fb2972a4653cc5476b946e5e304379795174647ee",
          "asset_sha256": "148837ba5f622a8cbbd275ef3da2a74eafb2cf4a6629b7cafa989635488b4ff7"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p14-andrew-exp-s03-c2-7af8feb0c302",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The application talks through a managed proxy in its task, and the target service's proxy handles the other end. The namespace helps with discovery; the proxies carry traffic on a network that still has to be reachable.",
          "text_sha256": "7af8feb0c302d9d2aac2d99bd811a84fbe85a7ae0b45a63cbbabf9f667649b31",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7af8feb0c302d9d2aac2d99bd811a84fbe85a7ae0b45a63cbbabf9f667649b31",
          "asset_sha256": "148837ba5f622a8cbbd275ef3da2a74eafb2cf4a6629b7cafa989635488b4ff7"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p14-andrew-exp-s04-c1-7d1123d5d381",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Configure the participating services to use the intended namespace and service name. Eligible services can share a namespace across accounts in the same Region when configured correctly.",
          "text_sha256": "7d1123d5d381ef6dccfb32f322397cc4b78d2d16682ad8f7a69c2f81c20e9724",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7d1123d5d381ef6dccfb32f322397cc4b78d2d16682ad8f7a69c2f81c20e9724",
          "asset_sha256": "b3f4519f7ea9747e3b6b3c7cce083c14be9ebcbadb207eba2763b9f48de205c5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p14-andrew-exp-s04-c2-91fe800f11ff",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Follow traffic from the app to its proxy, across the reachable network, then through the target proxy to the other app. Service Connect does not create a VPC tunnel. Verify routing, ports and security groups.",
          "text_sha256": "91fe800f11ff0073648c912c2d4235687799cf496615c3c65fddd07a1cb08e11",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "91fe800f11ff0073648c912c2d4235687799cf496615c3c65fddd07a1cb08e11",
          "asset_sha256": "b3f4519f7ea9747e3b6b3c7cce083c14be9ebcbadb207eba2763b9f48de205c5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p14-andrew-exp-s04-c3-ffc37343c7e2",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "If a client is outside the Service Connect setup, give it a supported ingress or access path. A short name inside the namespace is not an internet endpoint.",
          "text_sha256": "ffc37343c7e2a7c335b62f68fb5a6d0026f165f603e5486c79247240e976c2c0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ffc37343c7e2a7c335b62f68fb5a6d0026f165f603e5486c79247240e976c2c0",
          "asset_sha256": "b3f4519f7ea9747e3b6b3c7cce083c14be9ebcbadb207eba2763b9f48de205c5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "15",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p15-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "748169d1d39b71eb6554f2041e596a2078ca3d42e3cf275d4c885eb2bed2bd77",
        "2": "cb207686b307f54dd310c23595bcc0e54ebc7da209338b020e56f6733ccafdcf",
        "3": "407eac369236ec98e77c988c58bc0d512084c6a8d538025fc28384cbf16975bc"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p15-andrew-exp-s01-c1-39b2828009ac",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "App Mesh ended support on September thirty, twenty twenty-six. Don't choose it for a new deployment. The need to observe and control service traffic did not go away.",
          "text_sha256": "39b2828009ac6803c1940c39876dc2895df7665a0ee35b7377f23b304b0d3cfd",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "39b2828009ac6803c1940c39876dc2895df7665a0ee35b7377f23b304b0d3cfd",
          "asset_sha256": "748169d1d39b71eb6554f2041e596a2078ca3d42e3cf275d4c885eb2bed2bd77"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p15-andrew-exp-s01-c2-44bdb85fa4e1",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Before migrating, list the behavior the app expects: routing, telemetry, service identity, and retries. A retry can repeat a business operation unless the app is built to handle that safely.",
          "text_sha256": "44bdb85fa4e15dc43d4bd7d18da348ae473484e658957289f35d1c8ad09424d0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "44bdb85fa4e15dc43d4bd7d18da348ae473484e658957289f35d1c8ad09424d0",
          "asset_sha256": "748169d1d39b71eb6554f2041e596a2078ca3d42e3cf275d4c885eb2bed2bd77"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p15-andrew-exp-s01-c3-5d05823d30f1",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Evaluate Service Connect for suitable E C S communication, VPC Lattice for service connectivity and authorization, or an appropriate koo ber NET ees option. Verify the features you actually use instead of treating the choices as interchangeable.",
          "text_sha256": "5d05823d30f195e9a7345d3bbbe5b67d36e5fd11473e017f4c0510d6aed70e1a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "68d82ba9681b4e512a5186119993ed15b4cb8cf406cb7001442bb9dc65cbf643",
          "asset_sha256": "748169d1d39b71eb6554f2041e596a2078ca3d42e3cf275d4c885eb2bed2bd77"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p15-andrew-exp-s02-c1-84c080d03819",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The caller and target are in separate VPCs. Lattice connects an eligible caller to a service through its service network and sends traffic to registered healthy targets.",
          "text_sha256": "84c080d038195d43c412c9bdd8ab57fd3f53d7f56a6d4b38af04988c73654b79",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "84c080d038195d43c412c9bdd8ab57fd3f53d7f56a6d4b38af04988c73654b79",
          "asset_sha256": "cb207686b307f54dd310c23595bcc0e54ebc7da209338b020e56f6733ccafdcf"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p15-andrew-exp-s02-c2-eb7528723792",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Association supplies a network path, not blanket permission. When A W S I A M authorization is selected, check the policy and the caller's signed request. Verify the target responds.",
          "text_sha256": "eb75287237921ed95bf082d3d281c6a48b9abff6b7ad1709b527a6ae245cbe2b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5fb39e1b32f4d4fd23938916cca55fec0e0b1c382bf891d5ba8275ebab13d148",
          "asset_sha256": "cb207686b307f54dd310c23595bcc0e54ebc7da209338b020e56f6733ccafdcf"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p15-andrew-exp-s03-c1-01b0b4703e2b",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Can the caller reach the service network at all? Verify the intended association or supported connectivity. That test only answers the reachability question.",
          "text_sha256": "01b0b4703e2b485601b8035ed715223bb6948d838dd50f6ad3fe7a698aad1f28",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "01b0b4703e2b485601b8035ed715223bb6948d838dd50f6ad3fe7a698aad1f28",
          "asset_sha256": "407eac369236ec98e77c988c58bc0d512084c6a8d538025fc28384cbf16975bc"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p15-andrew-exp-s03-c2-a7c4069c426a",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "In A W S I A M mode, the auth policy and the caller's permissions govern the signed request. A caller with a route can still be rejected at this gate.",
          "text_sha256": "a7c4069c426a21f1cc66ba9df05e010f3ee19d0271f87c43b2a91a614fdf8871",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6a5c9add24aa92bdf78788db00649a7ae0784ae992d0c4b1f8757457c6db18f6",
          "asset_sha256": "407eac369236ec98e77c988c58bc0d512084c6a8d538025fc28384cbf16975bc"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p15-andrew-exp-s03-c3-8d66509048d0",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "A permitted request still needs a working listener and healthy target. Use the logs and health evidence to tell a rejected request from one that cannot reach an available target.",
          "text_sha256": "8d66509048d07ea2f7fa0ad797cf3f6574ed67d5af096daa406ca88dbc6ebcb6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8d66509048d07ea2f7fa0ad797cf3f6574ed67d5af096daa406ca88dbc6ebcb6",
          "asset_sha256": "407eac369236ec98e77c988c58bc0d512084c6a8d538025fc28384cbf16975bc"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "16",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p16-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "660d8f5feb72c6e60ba5452c9a85358e8640517b4806052edd2fce5e7e83c92b",
        "2": "5031c0e59e62ca8c70ba9bad64e71b650e5f177d50d6b9069d25ba95427c5211",
        "3": "58f960df3a5a2b4cb3056e9cf582b03286a201c34138c73b5a1cc0b4cc97983d"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p16-andrew-exp-s01-c1-a36a6d8ecbf4",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A higher-trust boundary is not always enough for a sensitive tenant. A silo gives that tenant dedicated resources, shrinking shared blast radius at the cost of operating more infrastructure.",
          "text_sha256": "a36a6d8ecbf4229ecedb8826463abbeaf7e0d632242f16c98d5ade9b69710fdc",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a36a6d8ecbf4229ecedb8826463abbeaf7e0d632242f16c98d5ade9b69710fdc",
          "asset_sha256": "660d8f5feb72c6e60ba5452c9a85358e8640517b4806052edd2fce5e7e83c92b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-andrew-exp-s01-c2-222896f338c8",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A pool shares more infrastructure. That can improve utilization, but the application must enforce tenant-scoped access and manage contention on those shared resources.",
          "text_sha256": "222896f338c8fd2a08aca1185ea0de502630da9dc6f0ec8ee95d5016c8aed51a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "222896f338c8fd2a08aca1185ea0de502630da9dc6f0ec8ee95d5016c8aed51a",
          "asset_sha256": "660d8f5feb72c6e60ba5452c9a85358e8640517b4806052edd2fce5e7e83c92b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-andrew-exp-s01-c3-ad1e320b5615",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A bridge keeps some layers shared and dedicates selected compute or data layers. Pick where the boundary belongs based on the risk and recovery requirements.",
          "text_sha256": "ad1e320b5615520eb63b6268c9c55d0a3ffdd428e011add511b867300aa0abea",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ad1e320b5615520eb63b6268c9c55d0a3ffdd428e011add511b867300aa0abea",
          "asset_sha256": "660d8f5feb72c6e60ba5452c9a85358e8640517b4806052edd2fce5e7e83c92b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-andrew-exp-s02-c1-b124465a73c6",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Compare a tenant in a separate account or cluster with tenants in a pooled app. Then consider the bridge option if selected data must be dedicated. The right choice depends on what must remain isolated when something fails.",
          "text_sha256": "b124465a73c60109f87742b768c9b7b58cb0937eee697dc81395f58fdd601721",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b124465a73c60109f87742b768c9b7b58cb0937eee697dc81395f58fdd601721",
          "asset_sha256": "5031c0e59e62ca8c70ba9bad64e71b650e5f177d50d6b9069d25ba95427c5211"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-andrew-exp-s02-c2-cebd975f1d5e",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Derive tenant context from trusted authentication and enforce it with scoped policy through to data access. A tenant I D the client provides is not proof that it can access that tenant.",
          "text_sha256": "cebd975f1d5e54e453e64b77c9ac7e63b6641d174806e9e88241e683dff2a339",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b238d8d7321f664fd7c3cc36c2ddc5ec26a7048a381f4ec3f8646cc3d21086ec",
          "asset_sha256": "5031c0e59e62ca8c70ba9bad64e71b650e5f177d50d6b9069d25ba95427c5211"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-andrew-exp-s03-c1-f2a1d9badac7",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "koo ber NET ees can put two apps in different namespaces while their Pods still share worker nodes and a kernel. A namespace helps organize access, but that alone does not make a hard tenant boundary.",
          "text_sha256": "f2a1d9badac7a29d9872ea4a23223710904eefe88bc0ef9610c4d8e6c70ca285",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "dd7a081c20556ef5da6c485e1756179b71541266107db9a53f5c50b261c74e6d",
          "asset_sha256": "58f960df3a5a2b4cb3056e9cf582b03286a201c34138c73b5a1cc0b4cc97983d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-andrew-exp-s03-c2-7b71f80056e6",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Use scoped koo ber NET ees permissions, admission and resource controls, network policy, and least-privilege Pod identity as appropriate. Check that each control protects the path it is supposed to protect.",
          "text_sha256": "7b71f80056e6e291f3e360c6340b37eaf8e10a1b4f5f102b6891b2f07e93860d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "13e121e6244b11510b74bfb83cf808e207cda12e5f44c8308f1a7296aab1fec5",
          "asset_sha256": "58f960df3a5a2b4cb3056e9cf582b03286a201c34138c73b5a1cc0b4cc97983d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-andrew-exp-s03-c3-26d9f9d0445d",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "For stronger separation, evaluate dedicated nodes, clusters or accounts based on the threat model. A dedicated node and a separate account are not equivalent. Verify the isolation and recovery behavior the design needs.",
          "text_sha256": "26d9f9d0445dc11104c8642ae67bc4ed5eed9b5906da45010c4974890d2b69b8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "26d9f9d0445dc11104c8642ae67bc4ed5eed9b5906da45010c4974890d2b69b8",
          "asset_sha256": "58f960df3a5a2b4cb3056e9cf582b03286a201c34138c73b5a1cc0b4cc97983d"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
